<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The machine's firewall (SPEC.md §spec:container-engine): SSH and Portainer's
  HTTPS interface, nothing else.

  This lives in /usr/lib rather than /etc because it belongs to the image.
  firewalld reads /usr/lib/firewalld/zones for default and vendor configuration
  and /etc/firewalld/zones for local customisation, so an operator can shadow
  this file by name without the image and their change fighting each other.

  Narrower than the FedoraServer zone it replaces, which uCore makes the default.
  Deliberately dropped from that zone:

    cockpit (9090/tcp)   - uCore's cockpit is a disabled-by-default podman unit
                           and nothing here serves it.
    dhcpv6-client (546)  - the cost is real: a network that hands out IPv6 by
                           DHCPv6 will not give this machine an IPv6 address.
                           IPv4 DHCP is unaffected, and so is IPv6 SLAAC.
                           §req:quality-attributes scopes this to a home network
                           that assigns addresses automatically, which is IPv4
                           DHCP in practice.

  What this zone does NOT do: constrain containers. A published container port
  is DNAT'd and forwarded rather than delivered to INPUT, so it never meets these
  rules. Portainer's 9443 is reachable because it is published, and the entry
  below is defence in depth and documentation. The control over Portainer's
  agent-tunnel (8000) and plain-HTTP (9000) interfaces is that neither is
  published - see kantainer-portainer.service.

  <forward/> is kept exactly as the FedoraServer zone has it. It is not a port,
  so it is outside what this zone narrows, and changing forwarding semantics at
  the same time as the port list would be two changes wearing one hat - with
  Docker's own FORWARD chains on the other side of it.
-->
<zone>
  <short>kantainer</short>
  <description>Container host: SSH and the Portainer HTTPS interface only.</description>
  <service name="ssh"/>
  <port port="9443" protocol="tcp"/>
  <forward/>
</zone>
